   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing Maimonides Educational Center to receive retroactive real\nproperty tax exempt status",
    "basePrintNo": "S6163",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6163-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6163\n\nSPONSOR: RHOADS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing Maimonides Educational Center to receive retroactive\nreal property tax exempt status\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to relieve Maimonides Educational Center of\ntheir real property tax burden.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill, authorizes the County of Nassau to accept a\nretroactive application for real property tax exemption from Maimonides\nEducational Center in the town of Hempstead.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMaimonides Educational Center is a not-for-profit tax-exempt organiza-\ntion that purchased property located in Nassau County at 2083 Seneca\nGate, Merrick, NY, 11566. The transfer of ownership took place in April\nof 2020 and an exemption was filed in a timely manner with the Nassau\nCounty Assessor for the 2021/22 tax year. As a result of being unable to\nfile for property tax exemption for the 2019/20 and 2020/21 tax years,\nMaimonides Educational Center was liable for more than a year of proper-\nty taxes, despite their not-for-profit status, therefore necessitating\nthis legislation. This, legislation would provide with an exemption from\nthe real property taxes pursuant to 420-a of the Real Property Tax Law.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThe specific pro-rata amount of the tax return will be calculated by the\nNassau County Treasurer's Office.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
